@h1 Colon-scatter h1@

In a @strong single-line strong@ body, tokens shaped @code id:value code@ with
@strong zero whitespace strong@ are lifted out as parameters; the rest of the
line stays prose. It is the lightest way to tag a node mid-sentence:

@@@pre
@figure src:lamp caption:"Second-order Fresnel" figure@
pre@@@

@code src code@ and @code caption code@ become params; anything else on the line
is the figure's body.

@h2 The strict contract h2@

Scatter fires only under an exact contract, and that strictness is deliberate —
it is what keeps ordinary prose from being mis-read:

@ul
@li The id is @code [A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_-]* code@. li@
@li The value is a bare word @code [A-Za-z0-9_-]+ code@, a @code "quoted" code@
string (spaces allowed), an @code _italic_ code@ or @code *bold* code@ run, or
any @@@code @node code@@@ (bare, parens, or with a closer). li@
@li There is @strong no whitespace anywhere strong@ — including between the
@code : code@ and the value. li@
@li The byte just before the id must be the start of the line or a non-word,
non-backslash character. li@
ul@

@@@pre
@thing name:Tauraj thing@
pre@@@

That lifts @code name code@ to @code Tauraj code@ (fixture
24-colon-scatter/body-scatter-single). A quoted value carries spaces:

@@@pre
@thing mode:"complex value" thing@
pre@@@

(body-scatter-quoted.) Multiple tokens lift while residual prose remains
(body-scatter-multi), and a repeated key is last-one-wins
(body-scatter-override).

@h2 Rich values h2@

Because the value may itself be a node or an emphasis run, scatter lifts them as
sibling content: italic (body-scatter-italic-value), bold
(body-scatter-bold-value), a closer-form node (body-scatter-node-value), a
self-closing parens node (body-scatter-self-closing-node-value), a node carrying
its own params (body-scatter-multiple-node-params), a node then a bare token
(body-scatter-node-then-bare), and overriding a value with a node
(body-scatter-override-with-node).

@h2 A space after the colon breaks the contract h2@

Add a space and the token is no longer scatter — it is prose again:

@@@pre
@thing key: value thing@
pre@@@

Nothing is lifted (fixture
24-colon-scatter/body-scatter-space-after-colon-is-prose, verified parameter
source "none"). A real inline node on that line stays a node; only the
scatter-lift is suppressed.

@h2 The escape opt-out h2@

To keep a literal @code id:value code@ in prose, escape the colon —
@code name\:Tauraj code@ suppresses the lift and the backslash is stripped from
the output (fixture 24-colon-scatter/body-scatter-escape).

@h2 The false positive h2@

The strict contract has one honest downside: a space-free @code id:value code@
buried in real prose still lifts.

@@@pre
@thing the variable name:Tauraj is bad thing@
pre@@@

That lifts @code name code@ to @code Tauraj code@ even though you meant it as
prose (fixture 24-colon-scatter/false-positive-prose, verified). Two fixes:
escape the colon (@code name\: code@) or add a space (@code name: … code@). The
same pattern bites URLs, ratios, and times written mid-sentence.

@h2 Common mistakes h2@

@ul
@li Writing @code key: value code@ (with a space) and expecting a lift — it
stays prose. li@
@li An accidental @code foo:bar code@ mid-prose lifting a stray param (the false
positive) — escape or space it. li@
ul@

